<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU beef package talks set to resume at 1500 GMT.</title>
<headline>EU beef package talks set to resume at 1500 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farm ministers were due to resume talks on a beef aid and production cutting package at 1500 GMT, one hour later than planned, EU officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Ministers, meeting in restricted session with only one or two advisers, will discuss a revised compromise text from the Irish EU Presidency.</p>
<p>Officials said the main outstanding problems concerned the allocation of an extra 500 million Ecus aid to beef producers affected by the mad cow crisis and a reduction in national quotas for the number of male cattle eligible for EU aid.</p>
<p>Only Spain would be granted an increased quota.</p>
</text>
